In short
--------
Greeny is free to use, and we want other homebrew to build on top of it. The core
(the app, the background service, the website, the achievement definitions and the
artwork) is not open source yet, mainly to keep the rankings fair while the project is
young. See FAQ.md ("Is Greeny open source?") for the reasons and the plan.

This short summary is not the license: the full terms are below.


What you CAN do
---------------
  - Download the official releases of Greeny and use them for free, for personal and
    non-commercial use, on a console you own.
  - Build integrations: read the files Greeny writes on the SD card, show Greeny
    achievements in your HOME menu, launcher, overlay or other homebrew, launch the
    Greeny app and use the Greeny name and logo to credit it, following INTEGRATIONS.md.
  - Use, study and modify the Tesla overlay source code (folder "overlay"), under the
    GNU General Public License v2. See overlay/LICENSE.
  - Help the project: test games, research new achievements, report problems, translate,
    suggest ideas and share Greeny. Thank you!


What needs written permission first
-----------------------------------
Unless the author agrees in writing (open an issue or ask on Discord, we are happy to talk),
you may not:
  - copy, modify, translate or redistribute Greeny or any part of it, other than the
    overlay source and what INTEGRATIONS.md allows;
  - publish modified builds, forks or derivative projects based on it;
  - reuse its achievement definitions, artwork, mascot, sounds or name, other than the
    credit that INTEGRATIONS.md asks for;
  - sell it or include it in paid products or bundles.

The integration permission does not cover the achievement definitions, the binaries or
the source code.


Third-party components
